# USER.md — About {{ primary_human_name }}

_This file is about your primary human, written by them (and you, as you learn). It's the answer to "who is the person I'm in relationship with?" It will get filled in over conversations and over time. Don't try to complete it in one sitting; the human's job is to answer prompts when they feel like answering, your job is to capture and curate what they share._

---

## Who they are

_Some questions for them to answer in any order, on any timeline:_

- **Name:**
- **Pronouns:**
- **Birthday:**
- **Timezone:**
- **Where they live:**
- **What they do for work / school / craft:**
- **A short paragraph about how they think:** _(Linear or nonlinear? Many parallel threads or one deep one? What kind of mood are they in when they're at their best?)_

---

## What they want me to know about them that I might not figure out on my own

_This is the open prompt. Anything they want to volunteer. Could be health context, family dynamics, working preferences, sensitivities, jokes, irritants, dreams. Whatever they want me to know that wouldn't surface in normal conversation._

_(Empty until they fill it. Leave the prompt; remove this italicized note when content arrives.)_

---

## Health (only if they want to share)

_Anything that affects how I should be helpful. Conditions, energy patterns, medications, accommodations. Nothing here is required; only what they want to share._

---

## Family + close people

_Who matters to them. Names, relationships, pronouns, anything that helps me know who's who. They can fill in over time as people come up._

---

## Work / projects

_What they're working on. What's load-bearing. What's a passion project. What they wish they had more time for._

---

## What they need from me

_The job description, in their words. Some prompts to find their way:_

- _What do you wish you had more help with?_
- _What's a thing that always slips through the cracks that you'd want me to catch?_
- _Are there places you'd rather I not get involved?_
- _What does \"genuinely helpful\" mean to you, vs \"performatively helpful\"?_

---

## Communication style

_What lands well, what doesn't:_

- _Do you prefer concise or thorough?_
- _Do you want lists, prose, both?_
- _Do you want me to push back when I disagree, or note the disagreement quietly?_
- _Are there words / phrases / framings you don't like?_

---

## How to help me best

_The "do more of this, less of that" section. Captures patterns the human and the being notice as they live together. Examples (yours might differ):_

- _Prioritize aggressively when many things are open._
- _Bias toward finishing over generating new ideas._
- _Call out fragmentation if I'm switching too much._
- _Respect non-negotiable anchors (name them)._

---

## Decision heuristics

_When the being has to choose what to surface or what to deprioritize, what's the order? Add as patterns emerge._

---

## Interests + hobbies

_Things they care about outside the load-bearing work. Coffee. Music. Trail running. Whatever. Helps me know them as a person, not just a task-list._

---

## Key patterns

_Things I should remember about how they operate. Updated as I notice. \"They're sharper in the morning.\" \"They under-promise on travel time.\" \"They circle back on Sunday afternoons.\"_

---

_This file lives. It grows as I learn them and as they share. There is no point at which it's \"done.\" Every entry is a small artifact of paying attention._
